---
layout: layouts/base.njk
pageKey: index
title: "Do AI chatbots repeat Russian disinformation about Ukraine?"
description: "Citere detects when a major AI assistant repeats a Kremlin narrative, attributes it to the network that seeded it, and remediates it. Open data, CC BY 4.0."
pagination:
  data: build.languages
  alias: lang
  size: 1
permalink: "{{ '/' | loc(lang) }}"
---
{%- set doc = copy.en.index -%}
<div class="stage">
{% set side = "l" %}{% include "partials/hero-mesh.njk" %}
{% set side = "r" %}{% include "partials/hero-mesh.njk" %}

  <div class="hero">
    {%- if site.current_run and site.current_run.label %}
    <span class="pill"><span class="live"></span>{{ site.current_run.label }}{% if site.current_run.markets %} &middot; {{ site.current_run.markets }}{% endif %}</span>
    {%- endif %}
    <h1>{{ doc.data.h1 | fill(figures) }}</h1>
    <p class="sub">{{ doc.data.lead | fill(figures) | mdInline | safe }}</p>
    <div class="cta">
      {%- if navigation.has.registry %}<a class="btn btn-p" href="{{ '/registry/' | url }}">{{ 'action.browseRegistry' | t }}</a>{% endif %}
      {%- if navigation.has.reports %}<a class="btn btn-s" href="{{ '/monitor/' | url }}">{{ 'action.latestReport' | t }}</a>{% endif %}
    </div>
    <p class="stamp">Updated <time datetime="{{ lastUpdate | isoDate }}">{{ lastUpdate | displayDate }}</time> &middot; Open data, CC BY 4.0 &middot;
      <a href="{{ '/methodology/' | url }}">How we measure</a></p>
  </div>
</div>

{% include "partials/home-evidence.njk" %}

{%- if site.used_by | length %}
<section><div class="cited">
  <p class="cap">Our data is used by</p>
  <div class="orgs">
    {%- for item in site.used_by %}<a class="org" href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.org }}</a>{% endfor %}
  </div>
  <p class="note">Shown only once an organisation has published or confirmed receipt — each name links
    to the specific publication.</p>
</div></section>
{%- endif %}

<section><div class="band">
  <h2>{{ doc.sections['band'].title }}</h2>
  {{ doc.sections['band'].html | prefixLinks | defangCopy | safe }}
  {%- if quoteFigures %}
  <div class="quote">In {{ quoteFigures.run_label }}, chatbots refuted pure inventions <b>{{ quoteFigures.pure_refuted | rate }}</b> of the time — and
    repeated the claims built on a grain of truth in <b>{{ quoteFigures.grain_repeated | rate }}</b> of answers.</div>
  {%- endif %}
</div></section>

<section>
  <div class="shead"><h2>{{ 'section.howItWorks' | t }}</h2><a href="{{ '/methodology/' | url }}">Methodology &rarr;</a></div>
  <p class="lead">Six steps, from the first question we put to an assistant to the re-measurement four
    weeks later.</p>
  <div class="steps">
  {%- for step in ['detect','trace','publish','report','confirm','remeasure'] %}
    <div class="st"><div class="i">{{ loop.index }}</div>
      <h3>{{ doc.sections['step-' + step].title }}</h3>
      {{ doc.sections['step-' + step].html | prefixLinks | defangCopy | safe }}</div>
  {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="shead"><h2>{{ 'section.whyTrust' | t }}</h2></div>
  <p class="lead">Every figure here traces back to the answer it came from. Every statement about a
    platform traces back to the message we sent it, and the reply.</p>
  <div class="grid4">
  {%- for item in trustCards %}
    <div class="t"><h3>{{ doc.sections[item.key].title }}</h3>
      {{ doc.sections[item.key].html | prefixLinks | defangCopy | safe }}
      {%- if item.href %}<a href="{{ item.href | url }}">{{ item.label }} &rarr;</a>{% endif %}</div>
  {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
